News for git-annex 10.20261026:

git-annex (10.20261026) upstream; urgency=high
.
  A security fix has changed git-annex's behavior in several ways when
  enabling special remotes. The new git-annex verify command needs to be
  used to verify that the configuration of a special remote is safe.
  git-annex will prompt in situations where that is needed.
.
  Also, changes to a special remote configuration received in the git-annex
  branch no longer take effect until git-annex verifyremote is run to review
  and verify the new configuration.


git-annex 10.20261026 released with [[!toggle text="these changes"]]
[[!toggleable text="""  * This releases fixes a security hole that allowed private data
    exfiltration from special remotes. (CVE-2026-112818)
    https://git-annex.branchable.com/security/cross\_repository\_data\_exfiltration\_via\_special\_remote/
  * verifyremote: New command, used to verify the configuration of special
    remotes is safe.
  * enableremote: Display configuration and prompt for verifyremote to be
    run. Until it is verified, the special remote cannot be used,
    and git pushes to all remotes will be prevented.
  * When a special remote has been autoenabled, allow it to be used without
    verification, but prevent sending annexed files or git pushes to any
    remote until it is verified.
  * After upgrading git-annex, existing special remotes will continue to work
    as before. If a special remote could have been configured by a third
    party, you should verify its configuration using the
    `git-annex verifyremote` command.
  * Changes to special remote configuration received in the git-annex
    branch no longer take effect until git-annex verifyremote is run to
    review and verify the new configuration.
  * init: When run in an already initialized repository, avoid
    autoenabling new special remotes, since files received from
    them could leak out via other git-annex processes running in the
    repository.
  * init --autoenable: Refuse to perform probably unsafe action unless
    forced.
  * Added remote.name.annex-verified git config.
  * git-annex.cabal: Added Memory build flag to support building with
    older versions of crypton that don't use ram."""]]